   * Security considerations and user permissions:
   *
   * Requesting users must be authenticated. The endpoint enforces visibility
   * rules: private lists and tasks are returned only when the caller is the
   * owner or an accepted collaborator. Public lists and non-sensitive user data
   * may be returned according to platform policy. The operation MUST NOT leak
   * private content (task descriptions, private emails) for resources the
   * caller is not authorized to view.
   *
   * Relationship to underlying database entities:
   *
   * This operation composes results from the following Prisma models:
   * todo_app_tasks, todo_app_lists, todo_app_todouser, todo_app_task_tags.
   * Implementations SHOULD leverage the schema's text indexes (gin_trgm_ops)
   * for performant matching on title/description/name fields and must exclude
   * records where deleted_at IS NOT NULL.
   *
   * Validation rules and business logic:
   *
   * - The request body accepts: query text, pagination (page/pageSize or cursor),
   *   optional entity filters (task,list,user,tag), and optional scoping
   *   filters (ownerId, listId). UUID formats must be validated for id
   *   filters.
   * - Results are paginated; use deterministic tie-breakers for cursor stability.
   * - Partial failures in composing results (one entity backend times out) SHOULD
   *   be surfaced as warnings while returning successful partial results when
   *   possible.
   *
   * Expected behavior and error handling:
   *
   * - 200: Returns a paginated container of typed search results
   *   (IPageITodoAppSearchResult.ISummary).
   * - 400: Invalid request payload (bad pagination or malformed UUIDs).
